{"c":[{"id":"ed4bea715f035ec4","sum":"Helper: script env names go in privacy-gate.ts; diff guard-adversary vs base before loosening a guard; MAX_WAYS 8; MAX_GENERATOR_VISITS. Oracle rules off FillTrace.owns; choices need whole units. VM harness pins caret-v2-host; swift-typecheck needs ~7 GiB.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"88157b71ed581d98","sum":"Helper: new script env names go in privacy-gate.ts processEnv()/HELPER_ONLY_ENV; await PageFocus.moved; diff guard-adversary vs base before loosening a guard; askValues needed in hello; MAX_WAYS 8, optionIs, visit-capped generation; close page sessions before shutdown.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"90e1c122d2365aa7","sum":"New helper script env names go in privacy-gate.ts processEnv()/HELPER_ONLY_ENV. Await PageFocus.moved in tests. Before loosening a fill guard, diff guard-adversary --verifier vs base. Value questions need askValues in hello; realfill-asks scores AskAsks.fallback as automatic.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"efc720c8ec4faf9a","sum":"host-env.test.ts scans only helper/src for process.env; privacy-gate.ts reads its gate names via processEnv() and HELPER_ONLY_ENV, so new script env names go there. Tests can await PageFocus.moved; EngineSession.onFocus discards that promise.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261008T094208Z-4d056099840ba76b","text":"host-env.test.ts scans only helper/src for process.env; helper/scripts/privacy-gate.ts still reads its build-gate names (CARET_INTERNAL_BUILD, CARET_*PRIVACY_RESOURCE) through processEnv() and HELPER_ONLY_ENV, so new script env names go there too.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261008T100347Z-137d3d2067c38ff7","text":"Tests can await PageFocus.moved for the walk/focus completion; EngineSession.onFocus discards that promise.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"49be5dc02d9c236a","sum":"G36: before loosening a fill guard, diff guard-adversary --verifier accepts vs base; oneOfSeveral blocks role-labelled people's phones. VS1: value questions reach only hellos declaring askValues beside askChoices; realfill-asks scores AskAsks.fallback as the automatic result.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261008T103008Z-ae509cb3a9a659fb","text":"G36: before loosening a fill guard, diff guard-adversary --verifier accept attempts vs base; oneOfSeveral also blocks role-labelled people's phones (recruiter: Wren Ng, ...). page-w3 1f flaked once in the full fast suite, passes alone.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261008T103634Z-919e960bf3dcead3","text":"VS1: value questions reach only consumers whose hello declares askValues beside askChoices; realfill-asks scores a value question's AskAsks.fallback as the automatic result and its scripted picks as 'after pick'.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"5dd3dcb4d8abfb74","sum":"VS1/helper: Disclosure caps at MAX_WAYS 8 (rebuilt minted requests need 'plan' shape); Ask value options state exact outputs (builders.ts optionIs); generation stops at MAX_GENERATOR_VISITS, not time; close page sessions before Helper.shutdown/Store.close.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"84a4af324deddcaf","sum":"VS1: Disclosure composes at most MAX_WAYS (8) ways; past that a text carries every reason, so a request rebuilt from verifier-minted parts needs 'plan' in its shape slot. Ask value options state exact outputs; stand-ins match them with builders.ts optionIs.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261008T103634Z-c66a1e426ad50081","text":"VS1: Disclosure composes at most MAX_WAYS (8) ways; past that a text carries every reason of its parts, so a request rebuilt after the verifier minted its parts as plan text needs 'plan' in its shape slot.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261008T103634Z-ffaa923aad520f1c","text":"VS1: an Ask's value options state exact outputs ('Proposed value: \"…\". Source: …'); test stand-ins match them with test/builders.ts optionIs, while a fill on focus keeps its quoted-candidate criteria.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"78a720eef0312ba1","sum":"Candidate generation stops at MAX_GENERATOR_VISITS, not elapsed time (no budgetMs or generator clock); a visit-cap stop still marks a partial window cut. Tests wiring page sessions into Helper close them before Helper.shutdown and Store.close.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261008T122806Z-20adf579b39b18f9","text":"Candidate generation stops at MAX_GENERATOR_VISITS, not elapsed time; no setGeneratorClock, budgetMs or --generator-clock override remains. stats.ms is diagnostic, and a visit-cap stop still marks a partial window cut.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261008T131449Z-7a0add213d3fc6e0","text":"Tests that wire page sessions into Helper must close those sessions before Helper.shutdown and Store.close; a scheduled trailing walk otherwise reaches a closed store.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0e934890a2410f1d","sum":"Oracle rules: not on FillTrace.owns. Choices need whole units; owner notes omit labels; notes cap 1200. Ghost offers fit before publish. VM harness pins caret-v2-host; signed app's agent drops args (launchctl setenv). swift-typecheck needs ~7 GiB.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"2cf1dc4e6316fecf","sum":"Oracle rules must not use FillTrace.owns (realfill seals requests first). Source-supported choices need the whole unit sent. Owner notes omit field labels; source_notes cap 1200. Ghost offers fit before publish; page fixes use pageInsert.replace.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"71e3e7853f09b491","sum":"Oracle and choices: realfill-asks seals requests before the canned oracle answers, so FillTrace.owns(req) is false there; keep oracle rules off the trace. A source-supported choice needs its whole unit sent, so only Asks naming the source window get unit-based choices.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261008T143933Z-2d2e0e57729d25b3","text":"realfill-asks seals each request before the canned oracle answers it, so FillTrace.owns(req) is false there: the oracle reads fill questions by their text on the scoreboard but by the trace in the vs1 kit (runB31). Don't make oracle rules depend on the trace.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261008T143933Z-70fb13e0b1aaff9c","text":"v2/choices: a source-supported choice needs its whole unit sent; a TextEdit note never fits an Ask that does not name it (prose share keeps half back), so only Asks naming the source window get unit-based choices. The user's request is always a basis.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"44883686663002a4","sum":"Owner notes (note-unit.ts) omit field labels; choices use windowUnit; source_notes cap 1200 chars (OutOfShape). Ghost offers are fitted before publish (GhostFit.wordsThatFit) so Tab takes what is drawn; page fixes use pageInsert.replace, never AX.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261008T160920Z-9fcd651bc6963d88","text":"Owner notes (note-unit.ts unitText) omit an editable field's label, so an owner judgement never sees 'Do not use' over a value; choices use windowUnit (title plus every shown text of the page) instead. Sealed source_notes cap each note at 1200 chars and throw OutOfShape above it.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261009T034106Z-c7a9a6930e557ee3","text":"Ghost text offers are fitted before publish (GhostOverlay.inlineText, PageInlineMachine.offer via GhostFit.wordsThatFit), so Tab takes exactly what is drawn; a page fix replaces before the caret with pageInsert.replace (units), never via AX.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"70e132a2c654a0a3","sum":"VM: h13 harness hardcodes caret-v2-host (commit must be on v2/host); a signed Caret.app's agent drops launch args, so launchctl setenv test vars. Typecheck: swift-typecheck (~7 GiB free) or swiftc CaretScreenCore+CaretHostCore in ~10 s. Onboarding copy: OnboardingCopy.swift.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"ed334c8ae8fc83ed","sum":"h13 VM harness hardcodes caret-v2-host and needs the commit on v2/host; swift-typecheck needs ~7 GiB free. A team-signed Caret.app hands off to its SMAppService agent, dropping launch args: in the VM, launchctl setenv CARET_TEST_HOOKS/CARET_GHOST_REPLAY first.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261009T034106Z-ca16ffafb65f3efc","text":"The h13 VM harness hardcodes caret-v2-host and requires the commit on v2/host; another branch needs its own harness copy. swift-typecheck refuses below about 7 GiB free disk.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261009T035706Z-bf989410ed1cf336","text":"PX1: an opened team-signed Caret.app hands off to its SMAppService agent, which drops launch arguments; in the VM pass CARET_TEST_HOOKS/CARET_GHOST_REPLAY to the agent with launchctl setenv before open.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"728708ae62c328b3","sum":"CaretHostCore imports only CaretScreenCore: swiftc -emit-module of it plus -typecheck of CaretHostCore checks in ~10 s. Onboarding copy is OnboardingCopy.swift; progress in onboarding-progress.json beside settings; the guide frame floats at .floating.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261009T035706Z-f12bef9f03696e08","text":"PX1: CaretHostCore imports only CaretScreenCore, so swiftc -emit-module of CaretScreenCore plus swiftc -typecheck of CaretHostCore checks it in ~10 s with ~2 MB disk when heavy builds are disk-blocked.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261009T035707Z-e1b452775b82ff9a","text":"PX1 onboarding: copy lives in CaretHost/Onboarding/OnboardingCopy.swift; progress (resume step, coach slip shown) in onboarding-progress.json beside the settings file; the guide frame floats at .floating beside System Settings.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"b089598bcab48e21","sum":"Debug socket needs --test-hooks or CARET_DEBUG_SOCKET=full; store build ID differs. v2/access lacks v2 CI files. Copy evidence before caret-heavy prune; stated Ask intents use maker 'scripted'. VERIFY_CUTOFF 0.75. Stop #21/#33: post-interrupt prefix never Caret's.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"74b3e10a2720c1ee","sum":"Builds and rigs: debug socket is full only with --test-hooks or CARET_DEBUG_SOCKET=full; store build's extension ID differs until its key lands; v2/access lacks v2 CI files; old realfill logs can't replay routeBetween; macOS 26 rig needs a memory file for Gemma.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"fcf84ccb0d6c698f","sum":"Acceptance builds gate debug-socket commands behind --test-hooks/CARET_DEBUG_SOCKET=full; uninstall leaves dev.caret.host's shader cache. Chrome store build's ID differs until the store key lands. FigureView freezes off screen; rest beats read figureLife.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"c55d146fc1f7fbe5","sum":"Acceptance builds answer every debug-socket command only with --test-hooks or CARET_DEBUG_SOCKET=full (else state and spend only). kit uninstall.sh leaves the dev.caret.host Metal shader cache in DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261009T045910Z-0e9f96548471c298","text":"Acceptance builds (build-app.sh acceptance) answer every debug-socket command only with --test-hooks or CARET_DEBUG_SOCKET=full since e0d39205; otherwise state and spend only, as a release build (DF1).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261009T045910Z-abba01c47d6ec6b1","text":"kit uninstall.sh leaves $(getconf DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR)dev.caret.host (a Metal shader cache) behind; DF1's VM run 20261009T044644Z-88912 found it after uninstall.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f1360355f32207bc","sum":"Chrome store build strips the manifest key, so its ID differs from extension/EXTENSION_ID until the store key lands. FigureView freezes when rendersOffscreen; rest beats read figureLife (.seeded/.frozen), glances figureTyping (SurfaceCoordinator).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261009T065942Z-e248ff8cee60b01f","text":"Caret for Chrome store build (pnpm build:store) strips the manifest key, so the store ID differs from extension/EXTENSION_ID until the store's public key replaces it; tabs was dropped because the http(s) host permissions already expose tab title/url (checked in Chromium).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261009T082841Z-10e03653f161cdd3","text":"FigureView freezes itself when rendersOffscreen is set (Gallery.png), so references never catch a rest blink; rest beats (FigureIdle) take randomness from the figureLife environment (.seeded/.frozen) and the slip's glance direction from figureTyping, set in SurfaceCoordinator.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"a659985946d05235","sum":"Oct 9: v2/access lacks v2.yml/record-snapshots.yml (carry from sam/v2/ci); pre-Oct-9 realfill logs lack Jev probabilities, so can't replay routeBetween; macOS 26 rig guest needs rig-run's memory file for Gemma, and AXRead falls back to the frontmost app.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"51e2d3b90ee1e1c7","sum":"A branch off v2/access lacks v2.yml/record-snapshots.yml (on sam/v2/ci). realfill-asks records firstGate (planner/ask.ts Gate) and logs Jev's probabilities; replays of logs before 2026-10-09 can't show routeBetween.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261009T082841Z-f6fa2a2274a3373e","text":"v2/access (2026-10-09) has no .github/workflows/v2.yml or record-snapshots.yml; those live on sam/v2/ci with Swift 6.3 perch fixes, so CI for a branch off v2/access needs a carrier commit with them pushed to a v2/** branch (and snapshots/record).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261009T105258Z-d4c8517ede3130a0","text":"realfill-asks.ts records firstGate per Ask (planner/ask.ts Gate) and now logs Jev's per-option probabilities in --log-jev; replaying a log from before 2026-10-09 can't reproduce routeBetween (readHead needs probabilities).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"4013df696ec0e1c0","sum":"macOS 26 rig guest: rig-run takes an opt-in memory file (4-12 GiB; Gemma 3.4 GB needs more than the 4 GiB default), and the system-wide AX element fails focused-element reads (-25204), so AXRead falls back to the frontmost app.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261009T094824Z-62ada46022b5500b","text":"rig-run takes an opt-in memory file (whole GiB, 4-12) beside display; ops/heavy seals it (c0afa4d1). The 3.4 GB Gemma model runs out of GPU memory at the default 4 GiB.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261009T094824Z-d932ee9a36702a5a","text":"In the macOS 26 rig guest the system-wide AX element answers -25204 for its focused element and app while the app's own element works; AXRead.focusedElement falls back to the frontmost app (DF1 run 20261009T091737Z-83186).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"fe983e39a4c72ac3","sum":"Copy evidence out before caret-heavy prune. Stated Ask intents: ask {maker:'scripted'}. kinds.ts/TypedValues.swift share word lists. VERIFY_CUTOFF 0.75. Stop #21/#33: post-interrupt prefix never Caret's; input sets mayIncludeInput. Conversation-half rule binds; gate first.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"47cd907afc4fed0e","sum":"caret-heavy prune deletes inputs/vm-job/runs (copy evidence out first). Ask's maker is heads; tests needing a stated intent use ask {maker:'scripted'}. kinds.ts readerValue and TypedValues.swift membershipNumber share word lists. VERIFY_CUTOFF stays 0.75 (needs ~100 labels).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"5b20009202fb8dab","sum":"caret-heavy prune deletes inputs/vm-job/runs: copy guest evidence out first. Ask has one maker (heads); tests needing a stated intent use HelperOptions.ask {maker:'scripted'}; heads never gives scope 'all', so next-page carry only comes from a scripted intent.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261009T094824Z-f579be04c067ac3a","text":"caret-heavy prune deletes inputs/vm-job/runs (the whole guest evidence); copy the run directory out before pruning an r2-vm job.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261009T105413Z-5b58229438c03538","text":"Ask has one maker (heads). Tests needing a stated intent use HelperOptions.ask {maker:'scripted'} (page-rig.ts scriptedIntent); heads never gives scope 'all', so page kind 'all' and next-page carry only arise from a scripted intent.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"3c167740aee70ffb","sum":"kinds.ts readerValue and TypedValues.swift membershipNumber share word lists (membership digit runs are ids): change both. VERIFY_CUTOFF stays 0.75: lowering needs ~100 labelled wrong answers in the band; W2 had 32 in 0.65-0.75.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261009T133022Z-c6da35b2ee65e6ca","text":"Reader typed-value kinds have a helper-side correction: fill/kinds.ts readerValue retypes a bare digit run on a loyalty/membership line from phone to id; TypedValues.swift membershipNumber applies the same word lists. Change both together.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261009T133022Z-f6d432411519e4b6","text":"VERIFY_CUTOFF (fill/contract.ts) stays 0.75 by the Oct 9 sweep: lowering it needs ~100 labelled wrong verifier answers in the new band; W2's dev-set run had only 32 between 0.65 and 0.75.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f8f0a73e598f6521","sum":"Stop (#21/#33): a prefix read after an interrupt is never Caret's; Esc may reach the page as input first, GoalRuns turns that pause into Stop. Half-of-a-conversation (limitOfTotal) binds B24-B31, not the caps. build-app.sh's first privacy gate stays before mode=, lock, mkdir.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"278d318cc8bd1bcf","sum":"Stop reconciliation (PR #21, #33): a prefix read after an interrupt is never Caret's; input evidence on the target since send (reader fieldInput, page inputAt) makes the read unknown and sets mayIncludeInput, so Undo refuses.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261009T113804Z-c650011b870c1da6","text":"Esc can reach the page reader as input before the host Stop: GoalRuns converts that executor pause to Stop, so in-flight write reconciliation must advance the step and preserve its warning across both boundaries.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261009T171711Z-0195578ee2d384fe","text":"Stop reconciliation: a proper prefix read after a pause or stop is never Caret's partial write (the user may have typed it); ledger partialWrite holds the exact prefix read before the interrupt, and undo restores only while the field holds exactly that.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"971ad19e10903c98","sum":"B24-B31: the half-of-a-conversation rule (limitOfTotal), not WINDOW_CHARS/CONVERSATION_CHARS, binds requests. build-app.sh's first privacy gate stays before mode=, the lock and any mkdir; gate calls prepend the pinned Node dir to PATH.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261009T173348Z-8c6aa59618126d59","text":"On B24-B31 the per-request reveal caps (measure.ts WINDOW_CHARS/CONVERSATION_CHARS) never bind: the half-of-a-conversation rule in limitOfTotal does (limits 342-560). Raising the caps alone changes no request.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261009T174852Z-a5c504b96c31ede7","text":"build-app.sh's first privacy gate must stay before mode=, the lock and any mkdir (test_privacy_followup, test_internal_build_gate prelude); moving it after the Node download (0e02442a) broke the python job. Gate calls prepend the pinned Node dir to PATH instead.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
